"<strong>Q5.</strong> Latent heat makes the white dwarf take longer to fade, yet at any given core temperature it is exactly as bright as without latent heat. Explain both facts.",
"<strong>Q6.</strong> A {#} M☉ helium white dwarf fades more slowly than a carbon/oxygen one of the same mass and radius, and does not crystallize within the age of the universe. Explain both, using the number of ions and Γ ∝ Z²/a.",
